      "title": "Paraguay’s president quits after millions of people’s savings frozen in bank crisis",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/paraguay-president-santiago-pena-resigns",
      "description": "<p>Santiago Peña’s rightwing administration had authorised Ueno Bank to drastically expand operations before collapse</p><p>Paraguay’s rightwing president, Santiago Peña, resigned on Thursday after a political and financial crisis collapsed the South American country’s banking system in recent days.</p><p>At the centre of the crisis is Ueno Bank, which in just a few years under Peña went from an obscure digital bank to one of the country’s largest lenders, claiming to have about 60% of Paraguay’s adult population as customers.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/05/paraguay-president-santiago-pena-resigns\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
